  abstract     = {Philosophy of language - Wittgenstein, Semantics,
                  Pragmatics: Frege's theory of meaning, for all its
                  sophistication, relied on an unsatisfactory account
                  of thoughts as abstract objects. The Tractatus did
                  not have to deal with such a problem, because it
                  treated meaning---and language
                  altogether---independently of the ways in which
                  language is actually used by human beings. Less than
                  10 years after the work's completion, however,
                  Wittgenstein came to believe that this dimension of
                  language is of paramount importance. Without some
                  account of it, he now thought, the entire system of
                  the Tractatus would collapse like a house of cards.
                  In writings and teachings from 1930 on, accordingly,
                  he emphasized}
}

